        .run(tauri::generate_context!())
        .expect("error while running tauri application");
}

spec.objective:
Fix 4 frontend safety issues from the audit of /home/morthos/projects/MySillyTavern (branch m25-tag-extractor). Files you own: src/ui/useAndroidBack.ts, src/ui/chat/ChatInput.tsx, src/App.tsx, and a new file src/ui/ErrorBoundary.tsx.

ISSUE 1 (Critical): `useAndroidBack.ts:48-63` — `window.history.pushState` is called unconditionally in the effect body (not in a callback), meaning it fires on every render when `hasOpenPanel` is true. This triggers `popstate` → `onBack()` → panel closes → re-render → another `pushState` — infinite loop that causes the black-screen bug.

FIX: The `pushState` should only fire ONCE when `hasOpenPanel` transitions from false to true, not on every re-render. Use a ref to track the previous value:
```ts
const prevOpenRef = useRef(state.hasOpenPanel);
useEffect(() => {
  const prevOpen = prevOpenRef.current;
  prevOpenRef.current = state.hasOpenPanel;
  if (!prevOpen && state.hasOpenPanel) {
    window.history.pushState({ panel: true }, "");
  }
  // ...rest of handler
```

ISSUE 2: No error boundary anywhere — any uncaught render error takes down the entire app.

FIX: Create `src/ui/ErrorBoundary.tsx` — a React class component error boundary with a fallback UI showing the error message and a "Reload" button. Import and wrap the app shell in `src/App.tsx`. The fallback should have the app's color scheme (use CSS vars like `var(--color-surface)` and `var(--color-text)`).

ISSUE 3: `ChatInput.tsx:224-228` — `__mstInsertPrompt` mutates `window` during render (not in useEffect). Double-fires in StrictMode.

FIX: Move the `window.__mstInsertPrompt = (text) => { ... }` assignment into a `useEffect` with an empty dependency array. The function body can use refs to access the current textarea and value setter.

ISSUE 4 (Medium): `ChatInput.tsx` — the insertRef useEffect doesn't clear after consumption. If the same ref text is sent twice, the second time it won't fire because the key is the same.

FIX: After consuming insertRef, call setInsertRef(null) or have the parent clear it. Actually, the caller (ChatScreen) already generates a new key each time. Verify this works correctly — if not, add a cleanup that resets after consumption.

VERIFICATION: Run `npx tsc --noEmit` after all edits.
